        366.7201232910156,
        106.36231231689453
      ],
      "text": "the choice of intravenous fluids",
      "font": "Helvetica-Condensed-Bold",
      "size": 22.0,
      "type": "heading_main"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        190.5670166015625,
        388.97003173828125,
        203.75601196289062
      ],
      "text": "12.1\t Choice of intravenous fluids for resuscitation and maintenance in",
      "font": "Helvetica-Condensed-Bold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        90.70870208740234,
        203.5670166015625,
        127.74569702148438,
        216.75601196289062
      ],
      "text": "children",
      "font": "Helvetica-Condensed-Bold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        220.19261169433594,
        399.052978515625,
        233.6826171875
      ],
      "text": "a)\t Resuscitation: Children severely dehydrated or with signs of shock should be",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        233.19261169433594,
        399.04156494140625,
        246.6826171875
      ],
      "text": "resuscitated using isotonic intravenous (IV) solutions such as sodium chloride",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        246.19261169433594,
        160.2314910888672,
        259.6826171875
      ],
      "text": "0.9% or ringers lactate.",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        261.5972900390625,
        252.91282653808594,
        275.5173034667969
      ],
      "text": "(Strong recommendation, low quality evidence)",
      "font": "MinionPro-BoldIt",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        277.86187744140625,
        399.12286376953125,
        291.3518981933594
      ],
      "text": "b)\tIntravenous maintenance fluid: For children who require intravenous (IV) fluids",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        290.86187744140625,
        399.13128662109375,
        304.3518981933594
      ],
      "text": "for maintenance, options include ringers lactate solution with 5% dextrose,",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        303.86187744140625,
        399.0813903808594,
        317.3518981933594
      ],
      "text": "sodium chloride 0.45% with glucose 5%, sodium chloride 0.45% with glucose",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        316.86187744140625,
        261.3315124511719,
        330.3518981933594
      ],
      "text": "2.5%, or 0.9% sodium chloride with glucose 5%.",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        332.2665100097656,
        252.91282653808594,
        346.1865234375
      ],
      "text": "(Strong recommendation, low quality evidence)",
      "font": "MinionPro-BoldIt",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        348.53118896484375,
        399.082763671875,
        362.0212097167969
      ],
      "text": "c)\t Low sodium-containing IV solutions such as sodium chloride 0.18% with glucose",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        361.53118896484375,
        399.0115051269531,
        375.0212097167969
      ],
      "text": "4%, or 5% glucose in water, should not be used as there is an increased risk of",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        374.53118896484375,
        132.15150451660156,
        388.0212097167969
      ],
      "text": "hyponatraemia.",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        389.935791015625,
        252.91282653808594,
        403.8558044433594
      ],
      "text": "(Strong recommendation, low quality evidence)",
      "font": "MinionPro-BoldIt",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        406.20050048828125,
        399.07281494140625,
        419.6905212402344
      ],
      "text": "There is evidence that there is a greater level of risk of hyponatraemia associated with",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        419.20050048828125,
        399.0627746582031,
        432.6905212402344
      ],
      "text": "the use of very low sodium-containing solutions in paediatric patients in comparison",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        432.20050048828125,
        274.7129821777344,
        445.6905212402344
      ],
      "text": "to fluids where the sodium content is 75–150mmol/L.",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        445.20050048828125,
        399.0314025878906,
        458.6905212402344
      ],
      "text": "The panel also emphasized that IV maintenance fluids should contain glucose to",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        458.20050048828125,
        399.102783203125,
        471.6905212402344
      ],
      "text": "avoid hypoglycaemia and starvation ketosis. Enteral feeding should be used in sick",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        471.20050048828125,
        399.10284423828125,
        484.6905212402344
      ],
      "text": "children, as it provides nutrition and avoids complications associated with IV fluids.",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        484.20050048828125,
        378.40289306640625,
        497.6905212402344
      ],
      "text": "If oral nutrition is not tolerated, nasogastric tube feeding should be considered.",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        508.7190246582031,
        231.48292541503906,
        520.7090454101562
      ],
      "text": "12.1.1\t Evidence and summary of findings",
      "font": "Helvetica-Condensed-Bold",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        524.3736572265625,
        399.0129699707031,
        537.8636474609375
      ],
      "text": "There is evidence of a greater level of risk of hyponatraemia associated with the use",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        537.3736572265625,
        399.10284423828125,
        550.8636474609375
      ],
      "text": "of hypotonic solutions: the odds of developing hyponatraemia following hypotonic",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        550.3736572265625,
        396.8504943847656,
        563.8636474609375
      ],
      "text": "solutions are 17.2 times greater than with isotonic fluids. Within the range of hypo­",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        563.3736572265625,
        399.07281494140625,
        576.8636474609375
      ],
      "text": "tonic solutions available, the use of sodium chloride 0.18% with glucose 4% presents",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        576.3736572265625,
        140.73289489746094,
        589.8636474609375
      ],
      "text": "an even greater risk.",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        589.3736572265625,
        399.0614318847656,
        602.8636474609375
      ],
      "text": "The panel identified a systematic review published in 2006 that sought to compare",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        602.3736572265625,
        399.0628967285156,
        615.8636474609375
      ],
      "text": "outcomes for children receiving hypotonic versus isotonic fluid therapy [Choong,",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        615.3736572265625,
        399.1328125,
        628.8636474609375
      ],
      "text": "2006]. The review included six studies: two controlled trials of children (1-12 years,",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        223.4420928955078,
        644.9403076171875,
        231.6051025390625,
        655.2992553710938
      ],
      "text": "79",
      "font": "Helvetica-Condensed-Ligh",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    }
  ]
}